# msl-seal-breach-mandatory-bakeout-15min

Cold Chain Rule 3: if an MSL dry-bag seal is broken for ANY reason (including re-taping), the lot must be returned to the bake-out oven area within 15 minutes, regardless of scheduled destination or schedule pressure.

## Procedures
- 1. If a dry-bag seal is reported broken or found broken, do NOT continue moving the lot toward its planned destination.
- 2. Immediately route the affected lot to the bake-out oven area — this must be initiated within 15 minutes of the seal breach being discovered.
- 3. Reject any operator or manager suggestion that 're-taping' or 'the parts are fine' makes continued movement acceptable — Rule 3 is non-waivable.
- 4. Notify Manufacturing Manager that the lot cannot reach its original destination on the original schedule; provide the estimated bake-out duration (typically ~24 hours).
- 5. Update IMS (per Rule 10: before physical move) to bake-out oven as new destination before moving the lot.

## Conventions
- Re-taping a broken bag seal does NOT restore MSL integrity — it must be treated as a full seal breach.
- Schedule pressure from manager or operator cannot override Rule 3.

